    ACP2E-5537: GraphQL addProductsToCart returns UNDEFINED for some cart validation errors
    
    Manual backport of ACP2E-5536 (be08a378368) to 2.4.7-p10.
    
    The automated backport failed because 2.4-develop resolves error codes through
    the DI-configurable errorMessageCodesMapper argument in Magento_Quote di.xml,
    while this release line keeps the mapping in the
    AddProductsToCartError::MESSAGE_CODES constant. The behavior change is ported
    into that constant instead.
    
    Mapped messages:
    - broadened "The requested qty is not available" to "The requested qty" so the
      maximum-qty-in-cart message resolves to INSUFFICIENT_STOCK
    - added "Not enough items for sale" => INSUFFICIENT_STOCK
    - added "You need to choose options for your item." => REQUIRED_PARAMETER_MISSING
    - added "The product quantity should be greater than", "You cannot use decimal
      quantity", "only in quantities of" and "Wrong format of the entered option
      data" => INVALID_PARAMETER_VALUE
    
    REQUIRED_PARAMETER_MISSING and INVALID_PARAMETER_VALUE are added to the
    CartUserInputErrorType and WishlistCartUserInputErrorType enums, because both
    user_errors fields are fed by the shared AddProductsToCartError and a code that
    is absent from the enum fails GraphQL serialization.
    
    "Only %s of %s available" is intentionally not mapped on this branch: it can
    only match once the rendered-number normalization added on 2.4-develop is
    present, so mapping the literal placeholder here would be dead configuration.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

